      },
      "message": "docs(site): Zola documentation site, deployed to GitHub Pages at each release tag\n\nA Zola project at site/ with our own templates (no third-party theme):\na user guide (install, first run, setups, operations, posting, reading a\nrefusal) and a short developer section (crate map, commands and undo,\ntest gates, releases), written from the README, AGENTS.md and the code.\nThe front page shows the version the site was built from and says the\nbrowser build is coming (#31).\n\nrelease.yml gains a `site` job (pinned Zola v0.23.6, checksum-verified,\nbuilds the tagged tree with the repo's Pages URL as base) and a `pages`\njob (actions/deploy-pages, pages: write + id-token: write scoped to it)\nthat deploys only on a tag once the release page is published. No new\ntrigger. site/public/ and site/version.toml are gitignored.\n\nRefs #688\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
